# The network of the BBR probe: a sender, a long and lossy link, a receiver.
#
#   shop 10.0.5.10 --- wan --- dr1 10.0.6.20
#
# The link is the path the Module 3 congestion designer measured CUBIC and
# BBR on: 50 Mbit/s, 25 ms each way (a 50 ms round trip), and 1% of the
# packets on their way to dr1 lost at random. shop sends the nightly
# archive; dr1 runs its receiver (iperf3's server, backup-sink.service).
machine shop
machine wan router
machine dr1

link shop:eth0=10.0.5.10/24 wan:eth0=10.0.5.1/24
link wan:eth1=10.0.6.1/24 dr1:eth0=10.0.6.20/24
route shop default via 10.0.5.1
route dr1 default via 10.0.6.1

# Towards dr1, where the data goes: the link's speed, its delay and its
# loss. Back towards shop, where the acknowledgements go: the delay only.
netem wan eth1 rate 50mbit delay 25ms loss 1% limit 2000
netem wan eth0 delay 25ms limit 2000
